abstract: >-
  Python implementation of Modular Time Field Theory (MTFT),
  deriving fundamental constants (α, α_s, sin²θ_W, particle masses)
  from arithmetic weights wₙ = Σ_{d|n} (log d)/d and the Feigenbaum
  constant. Includes a falsifiability engine with 23 zero-parameter
  predictions, lattice gauge theory, the Tano Mass Formula for lepton
  masses from X₀(143), and 21/23 predictions matching experiment to <1%.
